---
source: crates/cli/tests/it/help.rs
expression: long_help(path)
---
Run a dev environment per git worktree, side by side.

Every worktree of a project is a lane with its own ports, hostnames such as
web.acme-2.localhost and environment, so branches run at the same time. A
per-user daemon owns the processes and containers and keeps them running when
the terminal closes; this command and the TUI are its clients. Without a
command, devlanes opens the TUI on a terminal and prints status otherwise.

Usage: devlanes [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  start        Bring up a lane: infra, setup, tasks and services, then wait until ready
  stop         Stop units, or the whole lane when none are named
  restart      Stop and start units again with a fresh environment
  status       Show lanes and units with state, ports, URLs, CPU and memory
  logs         Read unit logs; each line carries a cursor to continue from
  wait         Wait until a unit or lane is ready or failed
  with         Start the lane, run a command against it, then stop what was started
  run          Run a task from devlanes.yaml and exit with its exit code
  exec         Run an ad-hoc command as a unit of the lane instead of backgrounding it with &
  attach       Attach this terminal to a unit's terminal; C-a d detaches
  ui           Open the TUI; closing it never stops anything
  lane         Create, list, clean and resume worktree lanes
  debug        Explain failures: why a unit is not up, errors, events and resource use
  env          Show, export or enter the environment of a lane or unit
  url          Print, open and list service URLs and routed hostnames
  infra        Start, stop and inspect the project's containers
  config       Validate devlanes.yaml
  certs        Trust the devlanes CA and install the hosts file writer
  secrets      Hand secrets from fnox to the daemon
  remote       Connect to boxes over SSH and mirror their lanes here
  daemon       Run, stop and install the background daemon
  doctor       Check the daemon, Docker, proxy, CA, hosts file and output mode, each with a fix; never starts the daemon
  completions  Print shell completions; lane and unit names come from the running daemon
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
      --json
          Print JSON: one document, or NDJSON for streams (same as --output json)

      --output <MODE>
          Output mode [default: agent when an AI agent runs devlanes, plain in CI or without a terminal, else human]

          Possible values:
          - human: Colors and symbols, for a terminal
          - plain: The same information without color, one line per event
          - agent: Terse lines for AI agents: failures first, with next commands, size-capped
          - json:  The daemon's data as JSON, or NDJSON for streams

      --project <PROJECT>
          Use this project instead of the one containing the current directory

      --lane <LANE>
          Use this lane ([project@]lane) instead of the current worktree's

      --yes
          Confirm actions that would ask first; needed when no terminal can prompt

      --quiet
          Print nothing on success; errors still go to stderr

      --env <KEY=VALUE>
          Set a variable for started processes (start, restart, run TASK, exec); repeatable

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Limit waits and streams, such as 30s, 5m or 1h [default for start and wait: 180s]

      --budget <BYTES>
          Cap agent-mode output at this many bytes [default: 16384, minimum: 256]

  -v, --verbose...
          Print timestamped diagnostics of the client and daemon to stderr; -vv for more [env: DEVLANES_VERBOSE=1|2]

Examples:
  devlanes start                                bring up this worktree's lane
  devlanes status                               lanes and units of this project
  devlanes logs acme@2:api --tail 200           last 200 lines of api in lane 2
  devlanes with --profile e2e -- pnpm test:e2e  start, run the tests, stop
  devlanes stop --mine                          stop what this agent session started

References:
  A lane is [project@]lane: a lane number (2), a branch (feat/checkout), a
  lane or worktree directory name, or a path. Without project@ the project of
  the current directory is used.
  A unit is [lane:]unit, such as api, 2:api or acme@feat/checkout:web.
  Commands that take several units also accept globs ("api-*") and tags (+web).
